pgrep -a name - finds the PID of a running process by name and shows its full command.

top -p PID - shows a live view of only the given process, with its CPU usage, memory usage, state and run time.

pmap -x PID - shows the memory map of a process, with the size (Kbytes), resident memory (RSS), dirty pages, permissions and mapping of each region.

long long counter - a 64-bit integer that holds the very large loop count without overflowing.

while (1) with counter++ - keeps the CPU busy continuously, which makes exp7a a CPU-bound process.

counter % 100000000 == 0 - prints a message only once every 100 million iterations, so the CPU is used for calculation instead of printing.

%lld - the printf format specifier for a long long value.

fopen(“dummy.txt”, “w”) - opens the file for writing and creates it if it does not exist, or empties it if it does.

fprintf() - writes formatted text into a file instead of the screen.

fclose() - closes the file and flushes the data to the disk.

sleep(1) - makes exp7b wait for 1 second after each file operation, so the process spends most of its time waiting and is an I/O-bound process.

#include <unistd.h> - provides sleep().
